        "id": 1793992
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T18:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Accessor MH need no more than 2 arguments: base (when it targets an instance field) and value (if it is a setter). \n \n`number_of_args \u003c\u003d 3` is a partially speculative: if more than 3 arguments are passed, then it can\u0027t be a valid accessor MH call and it does not matter much where MH object is allocated: WMTE will be thrown anyway.\n\nIf `number_of_args \u003c\u003d 3` and MH is accessor MH and types do match, then arguments are allocated to match a `DirectMethodHandle$Holder` method stored in `target` field.\n\nIn all other cases it does not matter where MH is allocated.",
      "parentUuid": "3014f4b6_3198865a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5985,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 5985,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "10e2816375f147d610a4cb2429b5ff868fb9b9fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
